decomposeHomogeneousMA -- Decomposition of one monomial algebra over a subalgebra
*********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        decomposeHomogeneousMA f
        decomposeHomogeneousMA R
        decomposeHomogeneousMA B
        decomposeHomogeneousMA M
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, between multigraded
        polynomial rings such that the degree monoids are homogeneous and the
        degrees are minimal generating sets of the degree monoids, or
      * R, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, multigraded,
        with homogeneous degree monoid, such that B = *note degrees:
        (Macaulay2Doc)degrees, R are minimal generators of the degree monoid,
        and set K = *note coefficientRing: (Macaulay2Doc)coefficientRing, R, or
      * B, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, with the generators of an affine
        semigroup in \mathbb{N}^d. In the case B is specified, K is set via the
        *note Option: (Macaulay2Doc)Option, *note CoefficientField:
        CoefficientField,. If a list of positive integers is given, the
        function uses *note adjoinPurePowers: adjoinPurePowers, and *note
        homogenizeSemigroup: homogenizeSemigroup, to convert it into a list of
        elements of \mathbb{N}^2.
      * M, a *note MonomialAlgebra: MonomialAlgebra,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note CoefficientField: CoefficientField, => ..., default value ZZ/101,
        Option to set the coefficient field.
      * *note ReturnMingens: ReturnMingens, => ..., default value false, Option
        to return the minimal generating set B_A of K[B] as K[A]-module.
      * *note Verbose: decomposeHomogeneousMA_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVerbose=>_pd_pd_pd_
        rp, => ..., default value 0, Option to print intermediate results.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, with the following data:
        Let B be the degree monoid of the *note target: (Macaulay2Doc)target,
        of f and analogously A for the *note source: (Macaulay2Doc)source,. The
        *note keys: (Macaulay2Doc)keys, are representatives of congruence
        classes in G(B) / G(A). The value associated to a key k is a tuple
        whose first component is a monomial ideal of K[A] isomorphic to the
        K[A]-submodule of K[B] consisting of elements in the class k, and whose
        second component is an element of *note ZZ: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ, that is
        the twist between the ideal and the submodule of K[B] with respect to
        the standard grading (which gives the minimal generators degree 1).

Description
===========



Let K[B] be the monomial algebra of the degree monoid of the *note target:
(Macaulay2Doc)target, of f and let analogously K[A] for *note source:
(Macaulay2Doc)source, of f. Assume that K[B] is finite as a K[A]-module.

The monomial algebra K[B] is decomposed as a direct sum of monomial ideals in
K[A] with twists in ZZ.

If B or R with degrees B is specified then A is computed via *note
findGeneratorsOfSubalgebra: findGeneratorsOfSubalgebra,.

Note that the shift chosen by the function depends on the monomial ordering of
K[A] (in the non-simplicial case).



