MonomialAlgebra -- The class of all monomialAlgebras.
*****************************************************

Description
===========

The class of monomial algebras K[B] where B is a subsemigroup of \mathbb{N}^r.

You can create a monomial algebra via the function *note monomialAlgebra:
monomialAlgebra, by either specifying

- the semigroup B as a list of generators. The field K is selected via the
option *note CoefficientField: CoefficientField,.

- a list of positive integers which is converted by *note adjoinPurePowers:
adjoinPurePowers, and *note homogenizeSemigroup: homogenizeSemigroup, into a
list B of elements of \mathbb{N}^2. The field K is selected via the option
*note CoefficientField: CoefficientField,.

- a multigraded polynomial ring K[X] with *note Degrees: (Macaulay2Doc)Degrees,
R = B.

This data can be extracted as follows:

*note ring(MonomialAlgebra): ring_lpMonomialAlgebra_rp, returns the associated
multigraded polynomial ring.

*note degrees(MonomialAlgebra): degrees_lpMonomialAlgebra_rp, returns B.

Key functions:

Decomposition:

*note decomposeMonomialAlgebra: decomposeMonomialAlgebra, -- Decomposition of a
monomial algebra over the subalgebra corresponding to the convex hull of the
degree monoid.

*note decomposeHomogeneousMA: decomposeHomogeneousMA, -- Decomposition of a
homogeneous monomial algebra over the subalgebra corresponding to the convex
hull of the degree monoid.

Ring-theoretic properties:

*note isCohenMacaulayMA: isCohenMacaulayMA, -- Test whether a simplicial
monomial algebra is Cohen-Macaulay.

*note isGorensteinMA: isGorensteinMA, -- Test whether a simplicial monomial
algebra is Gorenstein.

*note isBuchsbaumMA: isBuchsbaumMA, -- Test whether a simplicial monomial
algebra is Buchsbaum.

*note isNormalMA: isNormalMA, -- Test whether a simplicial monomial algebra is
normal.

*note isSeminormalMA: isSeminormalMA, -- Test whether a simplicial monomial
algebra is seminormal.

*note isSimplicialMA: isSimplicialMA, -- Test whether a monomial algebra is
simplicial.

Regularity:

*note regularityMA: regularityMA, -- Compute the regularity via the
decomposition.

*note degreeMA: degreeMA, -- Compute the degree via the decomposition.

*note codimMA: codimMA, -- Compute the codimension of a monomial algebra.







Methods that use a MonomialAlgebra:
===================================

  * "affineAlgebra(MonomialAlgebra)" -- see *note affineAlgebra: affineAlgebra,
    -- Define a monomial algebra
  * "binomialIdeal(MonomialAlgebra)" -- see *note binomialIdeal: binomialIdeal,
    -- Compute the ideal of a monomial algebra
  * "codimMA(MonomialAlgebra)" -- see *note codimMA: codimMA, -- Codimension of
    a monomial algebra.
  * "decomposeHomogeneousMA(MonomialAlgebra)" -- see *note
    decomposeHomogeneousMA: decomposeHomogeneousMA, -- Decomposition of one
    monomial algebra over a subalgebra
  * "decomposeMonomialAlgebra(MonomialAlgebra)" -- see *note
    decomposeMonomialAlgebra: decomposeMonomialAlgebra, -- Decomposition of one
    monomial algebra over a subalgebra
  * "degreeMA(MonomialAlgebra)" -- see *note degreeMA: degreeMA, -- Degree of a
    monomial algebra.
  * *note degrees(MonomialAlgebra): degrees_lpMonomialAlgebra_rp, -- Generators
    of the degree monoid
  * "findMonomialSubalgebra(MonomialAlgebra)" -- see *note
    findMonomialSubalgebra: findMonomialSubalgebra, -- Find monomial subalgebra
    corresponding to the convex hull.
  * "isBuchsbaumMA(MonomialAlgebra)" -- see *note isBuchsbaumMA: isBuchsbaumMA,
    -- Test whether a simplicial monomial algebra is Buchsbaum.
  * "isCohenMacaulayMA(MonomialAlgebra)" -- see *note isCohenMacaulayMA:
    isCohenMacaulayMA, -- Test whether a simplicial monomial algebra is
    Cohen-Macaulay.
  * "isGorensteinMA(MonomialAlgebra)" -- see *note isGorensteinMA:
    isGorensteinMA, -- Test whether a simplicial monomial algebra is
    Gorenstein.
  * "isNormalMA(MonomialAlgebra)" -- see *note isNormalMA: isNormalMA, -- Test
    whether a simplicial monomial algebra is normal.
  * "isSeminormalMA(MonomialAlgebra)" -- see *note isSeminormalMA:
    isSeminormalMA, -- Test whether a simplicial monomial algebra is
    seminormal.
  * "isSimplicialMA(MonomialAlgebra)" -- see *note isSimplicialMA:
    isSimplicialMA, -- Test whether a monomial algebra is simplicial.
  * *note net(MonomialAlgebra): net_lpMonomialAlgebra_rp, -- Pretty print for
    monomial algebras
  * "regularityMA(MonomialAlgebra)" -- see *note regularityMA: regularityMA, --
    Compute regularity from decomposition
  * *note ring(MonomialAlgebra): ring_lpMonomialAlgebra_rp, -- Multigraded
    polynomial ring associated to a monomial algebra

For the programmer
==================

The object *note MonomialAlgebra: MonomialAlgebra, is a *note type:
(Macaulay2Doc)Type,, with ancestor classes *note MutableHashTable:
(Macaulay2Doc)MutableHashTable, < *note HashTable: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, <
*note Thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,.

