monomialAlgebra -- Create a monomial algebra
********************************************

  * Usage: 
        monomialAlgebra R
        monomialAlgebra B
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, multigraded,
        with B = *note degrees: (Macaulay2Doc)degrees, R and K = *note
        coefficientRing: (Macaulay2Doc)coefficientRing, R, or
      * B, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, In the case B is specified, K is
        set via the *note Option: (Macaulay2Doc)Option, *note CoefficientField:
        CoefficientField,. If a list of positive integers is given, the
        function uses *note adjoinPurePowers: adjoinPurePowers, and *note
        homogenizeSemigroup: homogenizeSemigroup, to convert it into a list of
        elements of \mathbb{N}^2.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note CoefficientField: CoefficientField, => ..., default value ZZ/101,
        Option to set the coefficient field.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note MonomialAlgebra: MonomialAlgebra,, 

Description
===========

Create a monomial algebra K[B] by either specifying

- the semigroup B as a list of generators. The field K is selected via the
option *note CoefficientField: CoefficientField,.

- a list of positive integers which is converted by *note adjoinPurePowers:
adjoinPurePowers, and *note homogenizeSemigroup: homogenizeSemigroup, into a
list B of elements of \mathbb{N}^2. The field K is selected via the option
*note CoefficientField: CoefficientField,.

- a multigraded polynomial ring R with *note Degrees: (Macaulay2Doc)Degrees, R
= B.



Specifying B:



+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : B = {{1,2},{3,0},{0,4},{0,5}}                                |
|                                                                  |
|o1 = {{1, 2}, {3, 0}, {0, 4}, {0, 5}}                             |
|                                                                  |
|o1 : List                                                         |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : monomialAlgebra B                                            |
|                                                                  |
|      ZZ                                                          |
|o2 = ---[x ..x ]                                                  |
|     101  0   3                                                   |
|                                                                  |
|o2 : MonomialAlgebra generated by {{1, 2}, {3, 0}, {0, 4}, {0, 5}}|
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : monomialAlgebra(B, CoefficientField=>QQ)                     |
|                                                                  |
|o3 = QQ[x ..x ]                                                   |
|         0   3                                                    |
|                                                                  |
|o3 : MonomialAlgebra generated by {{1, 2}, {3, 0}, {0, 4}, {0, 5}}|
+------------------------------------------------------------------+



Specifying R:



+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : kk=ZZ/101                                                    |
|                                                                  |
|o4 = kk                                                           |
|                                                                  |
|o4 : QuotientRing                                                 |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : B = {{1,2},{3,0},{0,4},{0,5}}                                |
|                                                                  |
|o5 = {{1, 2}, {3, 0}, {0, 4}, {0, 5}}                             |
|                                                                  |
|o5 : List                                                         |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : monomialAlgebra(kk[x_0..x_3, Degrees=> B])                   |
|                                                                  |
|o6 = kk[x ..x ]                                                   |
|         0   3                                                    |
|                                                                  |
|o6 : MonomialAlgebra generated by {{1, 2}, {3, 0}, {0, 4}, {0, 5}}|
+------------------------------------------------------------------+



Specifying a list of integers to define a monomial curve:



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : M = monomialAlgebra {1,4,8,9,11}                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = kk[x ..x ]                                                              |
|         0   5                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : MonomialAlgebra generated by {{11, 0}, {0, 11}, {1, 10}, {4, 7}, {8, 3},|
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{9, 2}}                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use monomialAlgebra:
============================

  * "monomialAlgebra(List)"
  * "monomialAlgebra(PolynomialRing)"

